  "proposed": "Heading: Phone systems for tech companies: common questions\n\nQ: How quickly can we add new starters?\nA: In minutes. With a cloud platform such as 8x8 or Zoom Phone, a new user is added in the admin portal and signs in to the app the same day. When someone leaves, their number can be passed straight to a colleague.\n\nQ: Will it connect to the tools we already use?\nA: Usually, yes. 8x8 integrates with Salesforce, Microsoft Dynamics, Zendesk and HubSpot, and has open APIs if you want to build your own. Zoom Phone fits naturally if your teams already meet on Zoom.\n\nQ: Can sales and support run on the same platform?\nA: Yes. 8x8 Engage gives customer-facing staff outside the contact centre, such as account managers and customer success, contact centre tools like queues and call analytics. Your dedicated support team can run on 8x8's full contact centre on the same platform.\n\nQ: We have staff abroad. How does international calling work?\nA: 8x8 includes unlimited calling to around 48 countries on its higher plans, so calls between offices and to customers overseas don't add up. Local numbers in other countries can be added so customers there can reach you cheaply.\n\nQ: Do we still need desk phones?\nA: Most tech teams don't. A good headset and the app on a laptop is enough for most roles, and it works the same in the office or at home. Desk phones still make sense for reception and shared spaces.\n\nQ: Which tech companies do you work with?\nA: Our customers include Safecall, which provides independent whistleblowing services, and Smartdesc, an IT support provider for charities and non-profits.",
