  "proposed": "Heading: Business phone systems: common questions\n\nQ: Which phone system is right for my business?\nA: It depends on how your team works. If you live in Microsoft 365, Teams calling or Gamma may suit you. If you run a busy sales or service line, 8x8's contact centre features matter more. Our feature comparison lets you put the main platforms side by side, and we will give you a straight answer on the one that fits.\n\nQ: What is an AI receptionist?\nA: An AI receptionist answers calls and holds a real conversation, rather than playing a \"press 1\" menu. It can take messages, answer common questions and pass a caller to the right person. Holiday Taxis, one of our customers, runs 8x8 with AI to handle calls from travellers around the world.\n\nQ: Can we keep our existing phone numbers?\nA: Yes. Numbers are moved across (ported) from your current provider, so customers keep dialling the same numbers. We handle the paperwork and agree the date with you.\n\nQ: Do you supply mobiles and broadband as well as phone systems?\nA: Yes. We supply business mobiles, broadband and leased lines alongside phone systems and cyber security. One supplier and one point of contact makes problems quicker to sort out.\n\nQ: Can your systems handle outbound calling teams?\nA: Yes. Platforms like 8x8 support outbound and blended calling with call recording and live reporting. The Telemarketing Company, one of our customers, relies on its phone system for unscripted telemarketing and telesales.\n\nQ: What support do we get after go-live?\nA: 24/7 telephone maintenance and support from our own UK team. You speak to engineers who know your setup, not a general helpdesk.",
