  "pageTitle": "3CX",
  "link": "https://westpiertech.com/3cx/",
  "issue": "Add an FAQ block (7 questions)",
  "before": "Why switch to West Pier",
  "current": "(no FAQ on the page)",
  "proposed": "Heading: Common questions about 3CX\n\nQ: What is 3CX?\nA: 3CX is a business phone system you can run in the cloud, on your own server or as a mix of both. Call queues, recording, IVR menus and desktop and mobile apps come as standard.\n\nQ: How is 3CX licensed?\nA: 3CX is priced on the size of the system, based on how many calls can run at the same time, rather than a fee for every user. For many teams that works out cheaper than per-user cloud systems. We size the licence to your actual call volumes.\n\nQ: Can we host 3CX on our own server?\nA: Yes. 3CX can run on your own server, in the cloud, or on a hosted system we look after for you. If your call data needs to stay on site, an on-premise install keeps it there.\n\nQ: Can we keep our phone numbers if we move to 3CX?\nA: Yes. We port your existing numbers onto SIP trunks connected to 3CX and agree the switchover date with you, so you don't lose calls on the day.\n\nQ: Does 3CX work with Microsoft Teams?\nA: Yes. 3CX can connect to Teams so staff make and take calls in Teams, while 3CX handles the queues and routing behind it.\n\nQ: Can 3CX run a contact centre?\nA: 3CX handles queues and basic reporting on its own. For wallboards, call and screen recording, and AI quality scoring, we add Xima, which plugs into your existing 3CX system.\n\nQ: Do you support 3CX systems you didn't install?\nA: Usually, yes. We check the version, licence and security settings first, then take over support from there.",
