  "issue": "Add an FAQ block (6 questions)",
  "before": "Why switch to West Pier",
  "current": "(no FAQ on the page)",
  "proposed": "Heading: Common questions about Gamma\n\nQ: Who are Gamma?\nA: Gamma is a UK communications provider with its own core network. It supplies business voice, SIP trunks, connectivity and mobile, which businesses buy through partners like West Pier.\n\nQ: Can Gamma connect our calls to Microsoft Teams?\nA: Yes. Gamma offers both Operator Connect and Direct Routing for Teams. Operator Connect is the simpler route. Direct Routing suits businesses that need more control over how calls are handled.\n\nQ: What are SIP trunks, and do we need them?\nA: SIP trunks carry your calls over the internet instead of old ISDN lines. If you run your own phone system, such as 3CX or Avaya, Gamma SIP trunks connect it to the phone network.\n\nQ: Is Gamma ready for the BT PSTN and ISDN switch-off?\nA: Yes. Gamma's voice services run over IP, so they aren't affected when BT retires the old copper lines. If you still have ISDN or analogue lines, it's worth planning the move now rather than close to the deadline.\n\nQ: Can Gamma supply our internet and mobiles too?\nA: Yes. Gamma provides business connectivity and mobile alongside voice, so one provider can cover the lot and one support team looks after it.\n\nQ: What happens to our calls if the office internet goes down?\nA: Gamma services can divert calls to mobiles or another site automatically. We set up those failover rules at install, so callers still get through.",
