  "proposed": "Heading: Common questions about Zoom Phone\n\nQ: What is Zoom Phone?\nA: Zoom Phone is a cloud phone system built into the Zoom app your team already uses for meetings. Staff make and take calls on a computer, mobile or desk phone, using the same number wherever they are.\n\nQ: Can we keep our phone numbers if we move to Zoom Phone?\nA: Yes. We port your existing UK numbers to Zoom Phone and plan the cutover with you, so you don't miss calls on the day.\n\nQ: Can we use desk phones with Zoom Phone?\nA: Yes. Zoom Phone works with certified desk phones from makers such as Poly and Yealink. Many businesses keep a desk phone on reception and use the app for everyone else.\n\nQ: Does Zoom have a contact centre?\nA: Yes. Zoom Contact Center handles voice, chat and other channels on the same platform as Zoom Phone and meetings. It suits businesses that want one supplier for all of it.\n\nQ: What is Zoom AI Companion?\nA: AI Companion is Zoom's built-in assistant. It can summarise meetings and calls, draft follow-ups and answer questions about what was said. It comes with paid Zoom Workplace plans.\n\nQ: Why buy Zoom Phone through West Pier rather than direct?\nA: We build your call flows, port your numbers and train your staff. When you need help, you speak to a UK team who know your setup.",
